-- title:
--   Descended supersingular chart reduces to a quotient Drinfeld curve
-- statement:
--   Fix a prime $q$, a nonzero level $M'$, a valuation subring $A$ of $\overline{\mathbb Q}$ with residue field $\kappa$, a finite set $W$ of places of $\mathrm{modularFunctionFieldC}\,\kappa\,M'$ over $\kappa$, an inclusion $\mathrm{modularFunctionFieldBar}\,M'\le \mathrm{fieldBar}\,q\,M'$, a constant reduction $R_0$ of $A$ on $\mathrm{modularFunctionFieldBar}\,M'$ with values in $\mathrm{modularFunctionFieldC}\,\kappa\,M'$, a member $s$ of $W$, and the remaining rigid-descent data: an intermediate field $k_0$ of $\overline{\mathbb Q}/\mathbb Q$ with elements $\pi_0$ (lying in $A$), $\zeta_0$, $\varpi_t$, $\xi$, a natural number $\ell$, an intermediate field $K_b$ of $\overline{\mathbb Q}/k_0$ with a valuation subring $A_b$ cut out by membership in $A$ and an element $\varpi_b$, a prime $\ell'$, an intermediate field $K_{\ell}$ of $\mathrm{LaurentSeries}\,k_0$ over $k_0$, an algebra over $O:=A\cap k_0$ compatibly with $k_0$, a nonzero $j_\ell\in K_\ell$, an element $\varpi_t'\in O$, an ideal $y$ of the algebra of elements of $K_\ell$ integral over $O[j_\ell]$, an $O$-subalgebra $B_t$ of $K_\ell$ contained in a valuation subring $W_t$ of $K_\ell$, naturals $n,m$, $\gamma_0\in\mathrm{SL}(2,\mathbb Z)$, a $k_0$-automorphism $\tau_0$ of $K_\ell$, an element $\zeta_c$ of the adic completion of $O$ at its maximal ideal, the membership $\mathrm{jqNModC}\,k_0\,(q\ell')\in K_\ell$, an element $a_0\in O$, a finite set $\mathrm{ends}$ of subrings of $K_\ell$, and a witness $\mathcal F$ of the hypothesis bundle [`ModularCurve.FullLevel.RigidDescentHyps`](def/ModularCurve_RigidDescentHyps.html#L28) for all these data. Let $G$ be the subgroup of $k_0$-automorphisms of $K_\ell$ generated by those $\tau$ for which some $\gamma\in\Gamma(q)\cap\Gamma_0(M')$ satisfies `IsLevelAutAt` for $k_0$, $q\ell'$, $\xi$, level $(q\ell')^2M'$ with subgroup $\mathrm{levelH}\,(q\ell')\,M'$, the element $\gamma^{-1}$, $K_\ell$ and $\tau$; that is, $\tau$ acts on every quotient $x=f/g$ of modular forms of weight $k$ for $\Gamma_H((q\ell')^2M')$ with integral $q$-expansions ($g$ having nonzero expansion) by the slash action of $\mathrm{conjElemN}\,(q\ell')\,\gamma^{-1}$, after any embedding $\iota:k_0\to\mathbb C$ sending $\xi$ to $e^{2\pi i/(q\ell')}$. Let $K_0$ be the fixed field of $G$, let $B_0$ consist of the $G$-invariant elements of $B_t$, and let $W_0'$ be the valuation subring of $K_0$ cut out by membership in $W_t$. The assertion is: for every $\mathbb F_{q^2}$-algebra structure on $\kappa$ making $\mathrm{CoordRing}\,q\,\kappa$ a domain, there are a subgroup $C_s$ of the $(q+1)$-st roots of unity in $\mathbb F_{q^2}$ and a ring homomorphism $\rho$ from $B_0$ to $\mathrm{quotField}\,q\,\kappa\,C_s$, the subfield of the Drinfeld function field $\mathrm{Frac}(\mathrm{CoordRing}\,q\,\kappa)$ fixed by the $C_s$-part of the $\mathrm{hSubgroup}$-action, such that: $|C_s|=2\,\mathrm{placeWidthChar}\,q\,M'\,s$; the kernel of $\rho$ is the ideal of $B_0$ generated by the image of $\pi_0$; on $O$ the map $\rho$ is the residue map of $A$ followed by the structural map of $\kappa$; every element of $\mathrm{quotField}\,q\,\kappa\,C_s$ is of the form $\rho(g)/\rho(h)$ with $g,h\in B_0$ and $\rho(h)\ne0$; an element of $\mathrm{quotField}\,q\,\kappa\,C_s$ lies in the image of $\rho$ exactly when its image in the Drinfeld function field lies in the image of $\mathrm{CoordRing}\,q\,\kappa$; and $\rho$ is equivariant in the sense that for $\gamma\in\Gamma_0(M')$ and $\tau$ satisfying `IsLevelAutAt` for $\gamma^{-1}$ as above, whenever $(\mathrm{redQ}\,q\,\gamma,1)$ lies in $\mathrm{hSubgroup}\,q$ and $f\in B_0$ has $\tau f\in B_0$, one has $\rho(\tau f)=\mathrm{hFunctionFieldAction}\,q\,\kappa\,(\mathrm{redQ}\,q\,\gamma,1)\bigl(\rho(f)\bigr)$ inside the Drinfeld function field.
--
--   This identifies the special fibre of the $G$-descended supersingular affine chart of the modular curve with (the coordinate ring of) a quotient of the Drinfeld–Deligne–Lusztig curve $xy^q-x^qy=1$ by a group of $(q+1)$-st roots of unity of order twice the width of the supersingular place $s$, compatibly with the $\Gamma_0(M')$-level action. It feeds the integral-closedness statement for the invariant chart and the construction of the supersingular discrete valuation rings used in the semistable-reduction analysis of the modular curve at $q$.
